    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-49402",
      "aliases": [
        "GHSA-7xh3-mhg9-jcw8"
      ],
      "title": "Deno: Command Injection via spawnSync & spawn on Windows",
      "summary": "Deno is a JavaScript, TypeScript, and WebAssembly runtime. Prior to 2.7.10, Deno's node:child_process implementation provided an escapeShellArg() helper used when callers passed shell: true to spawn / spawnSync / exec and friends. On Windows, the helper failed to quote arguments that contained cmd.exe metacharacters and did not neutralize % (which cmd.exe expands even inside double-quoted strings). An attacker who controlled any portion of an argument passed to such a call could inject arbitrary additional commands into the spawned cmd.exe invocation. This vulnerability is fixed in 2.7.10.",
